  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q42-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "42",
    "prompt": "The graph of $y=\\log_2(x)$ is vertically dilated by a factor of $k$ to give $y=\\log_8(x)$. Find the value of $k$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$k=\\dfrac{1}{3}$.",
      "worked": "Replace $y\\mapsto \\frac{y}{k}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y}{k}&=\\log_2 x\\\\y&=k\\log_2 x\\end{align*}$$\n\nBy change of base, $\\log_8 x=\\dfrac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 8}=\\dfrac{1}{3}\\log_2 x$. Matching the multiplier gives $k=\\dfrac{1}{3}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
